                        <li><h2>Introduction to CSS</h2>
                            <p>Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) is a stylesheet language used to describe the presentation of<br>
                            a document written in HTML or XML (including XML dialects such as SVG, MathML or<br> 
                            XHTML). CSS describes how elements should be rendered on screen, on paper, in speech,<br>
                            or on other media. It is just a language that is used to describe the style of a document.</p>
                        
                            <h3>Basic Structure of CSS</h3>
                            <p>
                                h1 {<br>
                                    color: red;<br>
                                   }<br> 
                                where <b>h1</b> is the selector, <b>color</b> is the property, and <b>red</b> is the value.<br>
                            </p>
                            <h3>Simple Examples of CSS Properties:</h3>
                            <p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>color</li>
                                    <li>background-color</li>
                                </ul>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                        <li><h2>How to include CSS?</h2>
                            <ol>
                                <li><h3>Incline Styles:</h3>
                                    <p>Writting styles directly inline on each element.</p>
                                    <p>&lt;h1 style="color:red;"&gt;Apna College&lt;/h1&gt;</p>
                                </li>
                                <li><h3>Using &lt;style&gt; tag</h3>
                                    <p>Styles is added using &lt;style&gt; element in the same document in &lt;head&gt;.</p>
                                    <p>&lt;style&gt;<br>
                                        h1 {<br>
                                            color:red;<br>
                                        }<br>
                                        &lt;/style&gt;<br>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><h3>External Stylesheet <b>(Most Popular)</b></h3>
                                    <p>Writting CSS in a seperate document and linking it with HTML file.</p>
                                    <p>So, linking HTML with CSS file:<br>
                                        &lt;head&gt;<br>
                                        &lt;link rel="Stylesheet" href= "Style.css"&gt;<br>
                                        &lt;/head&gt;<br>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                            </ol>
                        </li>
                        <li><h2>Commonly Used Properties in CSS:</h2>
                            <ul>
                                <li><h3>Color Property:</h3>
                                    <p>Used to set the color of the foreground.</p>
                                    <p> color: blue;<br>
                                        color: #ff0000;<br>
                                        color: rgb(214, 122, 127);
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <li><h3>Background Color Property:</h3>
                                    <p>Used to set the color of the background.</p>
                                    <p> background-color: purple;<br>
                                        background-color: #00f0ff;<br>
                                        background-color: rgb(123, 155, 234);<br>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                                <b>Color Systems:</b>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><h4>Naming color:</h4>
                                        <p>color: blue;</p>
                                        <p>Each browser recognizes around 140 colors named.</p>
                                        <p><b>Examples:</b> red, blue, green, aqua, pink, yellow, purple e.t.c.</p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li><h4>RGB (Red Green Blue):</h4>
                                        <p> color: rgb(255, 0, 0); </p>
                                        <p><b>Examples:</b></p>
                                        <p>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>red: rgb(255, 0, 0); </li>
                                                <li>green: rgb(0, 255, 0); </li>
                                                <li>black: rgb(0, 0, 0); </li>
                                                <li>white: rgb(255, 255, 255); </li>
                                                <li>yellow: rgb(255, 255, 0); </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li><h4>Hexadecimal or Hex code:</h4>
                                        <p> Hex code consists (0-9) and (a-f)</p>
                                        <p>color: #ffffff; </p>
                                        <p><b>Examples:</b></p>
                                        <p>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>black: #000000; </li>
                                                <li>white: #ffffff; </li>
                                                <li>blue:  #0000ff; </li>
                                                <li>yellow:#ffff00; </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                                <li><h3>Text Properties:</h3>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li><b>text-align:</b> Left, right, center, justify | start (english) | end (arabic)</li>
                                        <li><b>font-weight:</b> How much bold, light should the text be?
                                            <p><b>range:</b> 100-900, <b>Normal:</b> 400, <b>Light:</b> x&lt;400, <br>
                                                <b>Bold:</b> x&gt;400</p>
                                        </li>
                                        <li>text-decoration:For line-through, down-line, and overline.
                                            <p>Sets apperance of decorative line on text like underline.</p>
                                            <p>
                                                Text Decoration: 
                                                <span style="text-decoration: underline;">underline</span>, 
                                                <span style="text-decoration: overline;">overline</span>, and 
                                                <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">line-through</span>.
                                            </p>
                                            <p>More common text-properties are: <i>text-decoration-color, text-decoration-line,<br>
                                                text-decoration-style (solid, double, dotted, dashed, wavy), text-decoration-thickness.</i></p>
                                            <ul><h4>Mostly used text-decoration:-</h4>
                                                <li>Underline</li>
                                                <li>line-through</li>
                                                <li>to remove default underline from anchor tag.
                                                    a { 
                                                        text-decoration: none;
                                                    }
                                                </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </li>
                                        <li><p><b><code>line-height:</code></b> <code>normal;</code> <code>2.5;</code> &rarr; It means <br>
                                            2.5 times the normal size.</p></li>
                                        <li><p><b><code>line-height:</code></b> <code>3em;</code> <code>150%;</code> <code>32px;</code></p></li>
                                        <li><p><b><code>letter-spacing:</code></b> <code>normal;</code> <code>2px;</code></p></li>
                                    </ul>
                                </li>
                                <li><h3>font-size Units in CSS:</h3>
                                    <table border="1">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Absolute</th>
                                            <th>Relative</th>
                                        </tr>
